{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551879-lay-off-at-chinese-room-before-bloodlines-2-release","id":1551879,"title":"Lay-off at Chinese room Before Bloodlines 2 release.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-26T20:08:05-07:00","id":1551879,"title":"Lay-off at Chinese room Before Bloodlines 2 release.","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/gaming-industry/bloodlines-2-developer-the-chinese-room-has-laid-off-employees-but-paradox-says-the-game-is-still-coming-in-october/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/NwmyXRxe3x47P4REKUQWaF-1920-80.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/gaming-industry/bloodlines-2-developer-the-chinese-room-has-laid-off-employees-but-paradox-says-the-game-is-still-coming-in-october/\" target=\"_blank\"> Bloodlines 2 developer The Chinese Room has laid off employees, but Paradox says the game is still coming in October </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/gaming-industry/bloodlines-2-developer-the-chinese-room-has-laid-off-employees-but-paradox-says-the-game-is-still-coming-in-october/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.pcgamer.com/gaming-industry/bloodlines-2-developer-the-chinese-room-has-laid-off-employees-but-paradox-says-the-game-is-still-coming-in-october/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A number of TCR employees revealed the layoffs on social media, and Paradox has effectively confirmed \"staffing changes\" at the studio. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So yeah like the title says bloodlines 2 dev the Chinese room has faced a wave of lay off before the games October release. Now apparently according to a Pradox rep said lay off won't negatively affect bloodlines 2 release.<br /> <br /> <br /> Still a studio laying off devs so they could make a bit more money is seldom a good look for said studio. Assuming bloodlines 2 came out in a good state that is...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T00:21:35-07:00","id":1551880,"title":"","content":"The article talks more about this being related to Sumo Digital:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The layoffs may be the result of ongoing struggles at Sumo Digital, which acquired The Chinese Room in 2018. In June 2024, Sumo Group laid off 15% of its workforce and closed Timbre Games, and then in February 2025 it announced a &quot;strategic decision to focus Sumo Digital exclusively on development services for partners,&quot; which it warned &quot;would have an impact on our studios and people.&quot; One of the employees posting about being laid off, Callum Munro, was a senior technical support at Sumo Group, a position that included providing on-site support for The Chinese Room. </div> </div> </div>But... I don't trust Paradox to not also be involved in telling Chinese Room/Sumo Digital to save money before the Bloodlines 2 release. We know from last year when higher-ups at Paradox called Bloodlines 2 a &quot;dead end&quot; and how they aren't interested in the game getting DLC. So that lack of confidence would line up well with them telling Chinese Room to cut costs by firing a few people who aren't needed anymore. <br /> <br /> And in the past Paradox has done this before. After Paradox deemed the launch of Harebrained Scheme's game &quot;Lamplighter's League&quot; a &quot;big disappointment&quot;, developers revealed this (<a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/paradox-says-the-lamplighters-league-sales-were-a-big-disappointment-confirms-recent-layoffs-at-developer-harebrained-schemes/\" target=\"_blank\">source</a>):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The failure of The Lamplighters League also brought to light reports of layoffs at Harebrained Schemes: One person claiming to be a former employee of the studio said on the Resetera forums that roughly 80% of the studio's employees had been laid off in July, and multiple former employees have said on social media that they had been let go by the studio in that time frame.<br /> <br /> The Paradox rep declined to provide numbers but confirmed that layoffs had taken place prior to The Lamplighters League's release, saying that &quot;Harebrained Schemes\u2019 staff was significantly reduced over the summer as the game entered its last phase of development and launch preparations.&quot; </div> </div> </div>So it wouldn't be unprecedented for these lay-offs not to be related to Paradox as well. Also, two of the biggest issues people had with Lamplighter's League were that it lacked content and was quite buggy at launch. And thanks to the lack of personnel, the latter couldn't be addressed quickly while since the people at Harebrained Scheme were busy fixing the bugs, they never found the time to give the game proper post-launch updates. Later Paradox had simply walked away completely from the project. <br /> <br /> Bloodlines 2 is looking better these days but the article does end on this ominous note of &quot;Even though October is now just four months away, a specific release date still hasn't been announced.&quot;. Even the Chinese Room version had been delayed two times already. Well, I guess we'll see in October what this game will be like...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}